Overpay and get the difference refunded!
Nanjing real estate market sees “difference compensation” again - ChinaNetNewsCenter
The Yangtze Evening Post/ZiNiu News (Reporter Ma Zuobow). On October 10th, during an interview, it was found that a long-missing "valuation agreement" has returned to the Nanjing real estate market. A property located in the New District of Jiangbei announced "price difference compensation," stating that other available units offer greater discounts than previous discounts prior to delivery, and that the developer is willing to swap houses and refund the price difference for buyers.
"Guaranteed Price Agreement" terms are not few
The property located in the New District of Jiangbei is called Poly Yanziyu Cloud Terrace. Mr. Sun, who was viewing the property, told the reporter that he found a "statement" last weekend when he was browsing the property.
The pictures he sent to the journalists show that the developer promises, for those who purchase properties between February 1 and February 28, that if any other units in the project are offered more favorable discounts (subject to being other unsold units of the same floor plan, building, unit, and property type), the developer may switch the buyer to another unit at no cost difference.
Sun said that real estate agents described it as a "price-lock agreement," aimed at making buyers feel secure in their purchase and not worrying about the developer lowering prices for promotional sales. "Now they're afraid that once they buy, it will be discounted. Go to the sales office to make a fuss there is no time, and not making a fuss also feels uncomfortable."
Yet, many homebuyers also feel that while such “price-lock agreements” offer buyers some reassurance, the conditions attached to them are not low enough.
Ms. Zheng, who plans to buy a first-time home in North Jiangnan, says that for insured listings, the first priority is the same floor plan, followed by the same building and unit. With so few comparable options available, the "barrier" remains quite high.
There are also buyers who argue that it is not easy for them to “fight for their rights” when purchasing properties due to asymmetry of information, as sellers may not exclude offering additional discounts during sales.
Whether buyers can be retained remains to be seen.
The reporter learned from Nanjing Online Real Estate that the project obtained a sales permit for two buildings totaling 252 units last November, with户型sizes ranging from 105 sqm, 114 sqm, and 129 sqm, and a full decoration sales permit average price of 39,843 yuan per square meter.
However, just two months later, online real estate shows that the total unsold units of this project currently stand at 157, accounting for 62.3%, with 128 units in Tower 8 having 113 unsold and 124 units in Tower 7 with 44 unsold. The total number of sold units is only 33, accounting for just 13%.
Market participants explain that "price protection agreements" also appeared in Nanjing in 2008.
In August of the previous year, the housing project Xiangtang Xiyuan on Huangshan Road West in He Xi had launched the "Price Guarantee Plan" to attract homebuyers. The details were as follows: "The company solemnly promises that if there is an increase in the discount within one year, any resulting difference will be refunded to the original owners."
Subsequently in April 2011, nine housing projects in Nanjing also offered some units for sale with a “price differential compensation” commitment.
The real estate market is warming up, and now more than ever requires a ‘shot of adrenaline.’
Mr. Shen, an experienced player in the Nanjing real estate industry, stated that “price lock” agreements are also one of the marketing approaches for real estate developers.
He believes that enterprises now need more confidence than homebuyers do, and that offering a “price-lock agreement” is essentially giving them a boost.
Regarding whether he can retain homebuyers, he says this depends on multiple factors such as regulatory policies and loan thresholds, and it remains to be seen at this time.
China's rescue team continues to carry out rescue operations in Turkey, rescuing 4 trapped individuals - Xinhua
Xinhua News Agency February 11 – According to a notice on the website of the Ministry of Emergency Management on February 11, China's rescue team, which was searching in Turkey, dispatched three operational teams and 45 rescuers on February 10, rescuing one person who was trapped.
Dispatched two search assessment teams to evaluate and investigate 15 buildings on Voddabash Street.
To date, four trapped individuals have been rescued, five fatalities have been identified, and life signs and risks assessments have been conducted on 25 severely damaged buildings.
The rescue teams will adjust their rescue forces scientifically according to the actual situation of the disaster area and on-site conditions, and carry out sustained and in-depth rescue operations.
The rescue team obtained rescue appeal information through multiple channels such as embassies, local governments, and UN relief organizations, and verified each case through online inquiries, on-site searches, and other methods.
Brief the Chinese Hong Kong rescue team on the current rescue environment and conditions of building collapses, and conduct joint search operations.
Currently serving as the Regional Coordination System (SSC5) with the Italian rescue team, and dispatching three members to work at the 5th RescEU Coordination Center. Communicating with multiple teams from countries including Italy, the United Kingdom, Serbia, Slovakia, and Oman, I have gained an understanding of the rescue operations conducted by both the UN rescue organization and various national rescue teams.
The rescue team continuously strengthens safety management and force support, adhering to the principle of "unified command, safety first," enhancing safety control at the rescue site, reinforcing requirements for rescue work discipline, and specifying safety precautions.
Implement continuous rotation on-duty and sentry work systems to strengthen camp security management.
Medical personnel of the rescue team provide daily health check-ups for the members to enhance medical safeguards for key personnel. Currently, all members of the rescue team are in good health, and they are conducting disinfection and sterilization of the camp area.
After establishing the campsite, the logistics support team erected a total of 26 jumbo tents across four categories: command communication, equipment storage, medical decontamination, and living accommodation, as well as dog kennels, to ensure the provision of over 30 sets of rescue equipment at the scene.
Kim Jong-un shows close interaction with his daughter while his wife is left on the sidelines.
(Comprehensive 11th Edition) North Korea held its 75th anniversary military parade on Sunday evening, with Kim Ji-won, the leader Kim Jong-un's daughter, not only attending but also standing alongside her father on the rostrum.
North Korean state media released footage on Sunday showing Kim Ju-ah hugging her father close, making affectionate eye contact and whispering to him several times. She gently held her father's cheek with her hands, even touching his chest. The father-and-daughter interaction was broadcast to the whole country.
However, First Lady Li Xuezhu could only step aside.
According to reports from "The Korean People's Newspaper" and others, on the official photo taken by Kim Jong-un and Lee Seo-ju couple on their daughter Kim Ji-ae’s 7th birthday dinner, Kim Ji-ae was seen sitting in the middle C seat, which is rarely seen. Moreover, on the 75th anniversary of the Army Day military parade the following evening, she was seen alongside Kim Jong-un on the dais together.
North Korean state media, CCTV of the Democratic People's Republic of Korea, later released footage of the parade, revealing more scenes of father-daughter affection.
Kim Jong-un looked several times at his daughter on the stage of the chairman table, with smiles never fading from their faces. They whispered to each other in their ears as well. At one point, Kim Chong-un cupped both cheeks of his father affectionately, and Kim Jong-un responded with a beaming smile.
Other state media images show that during times when Kingmu-ae is sitting on an indoor sofa with Kim Jong-un, she constantly touches her father’s face with her hand; and when she walks alongside her father, she touches Kim Jong-un’s chest with her hand.
And First Lady Li Xuequ only walked behind or sat on the side of her husband and daughter, always maintaining a few steps distance from them.
Korean media noted that since Kim Jong-un first appeared in public last November 18, when he tested the Hwasong-17 missile, his visibility has been increasing over the past three months, and he has now appeared at official events five times so far.
North Korean state media used honorifics such as "dearest heir" and "exalted heir" when mentioning Kim Chuwai, and broadcast clips of Kim Chuwai repeatedly shouting his unwavering support for white-blooded lineage while overlooking the parade from the stands.
These signs raise doubts about Kim Gu-ae’s pre-arranged succession to the Kim regime, with The Washington Post analyzing it as “a signal from Kim Jong-un elevating his middle-aged daughter to the position of successor.” However, others argue that such a conclusion is too hasty, noting that there are still various possibilities given that Kim Jong-un has a son.
"The Fund E Account" is here: The CSRC authorizes development, allowing all of an investor's funds under management to be pooled and queried - Economic Observation Net - Professional Financial News Website
Chinese news reporter Chen Shan raises the question: Is the difficulty in aggregating account information due to the complex channels for purchasing funds?
Always forgetting about the "slush fund"?
The issues of the villagers will soon be resolved.
On February 10, the CSRC announced that the "Fund E Account" APP has been made available on various mobile app stores and is currently undergoing public trial operation.
According to the introduction, the "Fund E Account" provides a one-stop service for individual investors to query information about public fund accounts and holdings, aiming to address industry pain points such as investors forgetting their accounts or finding it cumbersome to inquire.
According to data from Wind, as of the end of 2022, there were 156 fund management companies in China, managing a fund size of approximately 26 trillion yuan; there were 167 fund share registration institutions, and 411 fund sales institutions.
Each share registration institution has an independent account system and there is no industry-wide unified query channel.
Industry sources indicate that at the end of 2021, China's fund investors exceeded 720 million people, meaning half of the country’s population had invested in fund products.
Previously, investors had to check their purchase status with different sales institutions individually, but through the “Fund E Account,” all sales channels can be queried, making it clear at a glance how many funds they hold.
"What is the 'Fund E Account' APP?"
According to relevant documents, "Fund E Account" APP is a mobile application developed and constructed by CSRC with approval from the China Securities Regulatory Commission, providing one-stop query of the status of off-exchange shares of all-mutual-fund products for investors.
Investors can conveniently and quickly track their holdings of open-end fund shares from various fund managers across the market through the 'Fund E Account', enhancing query efficiency overall.
Specifically, investors can query through the “Fund E Account” information including: fund account information opened with all public offering fund managers, trading account information opened with public offering fund sales institutions, and the holdings of products such as open-end shares of publicly offered securities investment funds and collective asset management plans established by securities companies where the number of investors is not subject to a limit of 200 people.
Li Yuqian, business head of Shanghai Stock Exchange Fund Evaluation Research Center, told Economic Observer that investors can gain access to their holdings of all off-exchange public funds through the "Fund E Account" App in one-stop fashion. It helps investors recover "forgotten assets," and more importantly, it consolidates comprehensive fund investment information across multiple accounts for clients, enabling them to better track their investment status in real time, accurately, and comprehensively. This aids clients in optimizing their fund portfolio more effectively and better planning their financial arrangements.
How to register and use?
The reporter noted that as of now, the "Fund E Account" app is available in the app stores of Huawei, Apple, Xiaomi, OPPO, and vivo, but the app is still in an open trial-run phase. Registration requires filling out an invite code, and investors can contact the fund management company they hold to obtain it.
A customer service staff from a mid-to-large-sized public fund management company in Shanghai provided a six-digit invitation code to an Economic Observer reporter and said, "During the beta testing phase of the app, China Securities Clearing provides each fund manager with a certain number of invitation codes. Investors can call to obtain them, and we provide them all."
Users will no longer need an invite code to register when open registration is enabled after the trial run is over.
Please provide the Chinese text you would like translated.
The reporter registered and completed a query of their account by downloading and using the related documents posted on the CSRC website, which is titled "Fund E Account." The entire process took only a few minutes and mainly consisted of four steps: user registration, real-name authentication, binding of fund accounts, and querying public offering funds.
After completing the real-name authentication, click on the "Assets" fund binding button. All fund products purchased through various fund sales platforms by the journalist will be listed in the binding option list (accounts that can be bound). After binding, one can see the total assets of the invested funds and start using the query function.
Notably, the “Fund E Account” provides query services for investors and does not facilitate subscription, redemption, or trading.
The data displayed in the "Fund E Account" generally corresponds to the date three trading days prior to the date of the query (T day).
For instance, when opening the “Fund E Account” on February 10, the total assets, fund units held, and fund net asset value shown on the Assets page correspond to the date three trading days prior, which is February 7.
