While the names are the same, please be cautious and also kindly ask Amazon's representative to replace the correct image promptly. Thank you very much.
The worst online shopping experience
After placing the order on September 28th, the system showed it had been shipped, but I did not receive the goods until October 12th.
Checking the status of an Amazon order, the seller did not provide a shipping label number, and I can't track where the order is.
So I sent an email to the seller asking if they could provide a shipping tracking number, but got no response for two days.
Desperate, I contacted Amazon's customer service, who provided the seller's phone number. I then called the store and after a few attempts, the line connected. They informed me that the package had been lost and that they could have another one sent to me immediately.
Although I was very angry, since the computer was urgently needed, I didn't say much to the seller and just asked for it to be sent to me immediately.
So, the next day, I called to ask if it had shipped yet?
Seller says it's not available yet; it will be shipped in the afternoon.
I called again in the afternoon, and the seller said they would definitely ship it, with shipping after 5 or 6 PM. By the time I called at 7 PM, there was no answer on the phone.
On the third morning, I called again to ask if the shipment had been sent out?
May I have the order number now?
The seller said they haven't shipped yet. They told me that if I need it urgently, I can order from another seller, or if it's okay to wait, it will be shipped in the afternoon.
There's nothing I can do; placing an order from another place will take much longer.
All I can do is beg the seller to ship out quickly.
Finally, after countless phone trackings, I received the computer on October 16.
