The items are still good, but Amazon's customer service is much worse than that of other websites.
After placing the order, I found that I had ordered the wrong item, but the order cannot be canceled anymore. Trying to contact online customer service via the webpage keeps showing an incorrect link and I can't reach them.
After I received the delivery, the delivery person called me. I said I didn’t want it and that I hadn’t canceled the order successfully; therefore, the delivery person took it back and told me to sign for it first before applying for a refund.
When returning or exchanging items, they only inform us that food products cannot be returned once received; this is the same statement that they give when we say we cannot contact Amazon customer service because we have already received the item and it cannot be returned.
I have bought items that cannot be returned under policy from both JD and Suning before, including milk and diapers, and contacted customer service in both cases where they were able to get a refund. Even for diapers from JD that had an overwhelming odor after opening, I was able to get a refund through customer service. However, at Amazon, this doesn't work for me.
The rules are dead, people are alive. How did you handle contacting your customer service?
Tell me to either take it myself or let the delivery person buy it themselves. After all, delivery people don't have an easy job; why should I make them pay for something they didn't purchase?
Okay, I won’t back out either. I’ll take it, but I must give your service a score of 1 out of 5.
Amazon's own-brand should not carry such products.
Buy during product sales when the price is not low; it's also a good product based on reviews.
Upon receiving the actual product, I was stunned. The surface of the item had extensive wear and tear, and there were other areas of wear and tear as well. It was either a second-hand item or old, and I will post some pictures later.
I am returning the product, and after seeing the pictures, the personnel from the manufacturer said it was due to transportation damage. Isn't this just making things up?
How could there be wear and tear within the product?
There are only two possibilities: either defective or used items, or I intentionally damaged the product and returned it.
Objectively, I have no evidence to prove that I didn't damage the item. However, given my shopping history on Amazon, I believe such an item shouldn't be present in Amazon's own-brand products. Customers choose Amazon's own-brand because they trust it - customer wins, we win. The victory of the customer is also the victory of the manufacturer. Let's all work together to improve. Thank you.
A satisfactory watch
It's definitely genuine; I've checked the authenticity at the boutique. The appearance of the watch is very nice, and the workmanship is meticulous with ample materials. With an imported mechanical movement, it has some weight to it, which cannot be compared to those 300-400 yuan so-called mechanical watches. This one is of true value and quality.
The watch keeps accurate time with errors within acceptable limits. There is a gemstone appraisal certificate inside the watch box. The twelve o'clock position on the dial features real diamonds; it is suitable to wear and makes for a good gift.
The Bentley meter is quite good.
Compact and large capacity
Its lightness and large opening are nice to me, but two separate compartment bags feel a bit redundant; I'm not sure what to put in them.
After buying, I found that there was another brand similar product on Overseas Purchase from Meijia for less than 200 yuan.
The first time I bought it, everything was faulty; all the lights were flashing and it didn't work.
Requesting a return, but the shipment to Shanghai is already three days old and hasn't been sent over.
The call to delivery doesn't answer.
The courier company says they only have that contact information.
Amazon has no place to report complaints.
No request was made, and I received a message saying deliveries were being delayed for no reason, just as per my request.
What else was said about transshipment issues.
A poor shopping experience makes me doubt the effectiveness of Amazon's logistics and control systems.
Estimate that I won't be able to get it today either.
